{"agent":"fx-rules-fresh","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The filter `not GI.always(r) or GI.pinned(r)` keeps a rule that is both always-scope and pinned. The function’s own docstring says that when the charter is present, “a rule that applies to all work is left to it,” so that rule is already emitted by `CH.block`. For a rule record with `GI.always(r) == True` and `GI.pinned(r) == True`, the brief therefore contains the same rule line twice: once in the charter and once in the item-specific rules block. That duplication consumes an extra line of the `session.brief_max_tokens` budget for one record even though the code claims to leave always-scope rules to the charter. The filter should drop all `GI.always` records when the charter carries them, or use the exact set of rule ids `CH.block` actually emitted.","digest":"a23bd0633f021002","location":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/brief.py:_rules_block","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/brief.py:_rules_block"},{"chunk":5,"detail":"The `charter` text is appended before the existing backstop truncation, but the backstop is explicitly designed for the case where `_fit_sections` returns a body over its `room` because a single heading alone exceeded its share. In that case `charter` is the trailing part of `text`, and `text = text[: max(0, budget * 4 - len(note))].rsplit(\"\\n\", 1)[0]` truncates from the right, discarding the charter before the truncation note is appended. This means the `set_aside` reservation does not actually protect the pinned always-scope rules when the budget is tight enough to hit the existing backstop; the brief returns without the required rule titles, contrary to the intent that pinned always-scope rules never be trimmed.","digest":"8b9b874b2506475d","location":"ddflow/views/markdown.py:1127","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/views/markdown.py:1127"},{"chunk":6,"detail":"`pinned = GuidanceRecord(..., title=\"Pinned law\", ...)` uses a capital **P**, but the assertion checks for the lowercase substring `\"pinned\"`. A charter line rendered as `[r-pin] Pinned law` does not contain `\"pinned\"`, so this test fails on the fixed formatter even though the pinned rule is actually present. The check should be `\"Pinned\"` (or only `\"r-pin\" in got[0]`).","digest":"b477c237e16d5124","location":"tests/test_guidance_budget.py:56","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_guidance_budget.py:56"}],"chunks_total":6,"coverage":"6/6 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":21502,"diff_sha":"bc64b76dbbe16fe4b9de3f82660d93d642ffa9b33f9b41efb7a17e74f5385716","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":597.0,"excluded_bytes":1211185,"excluded_files":3,"excluded_paths":["README.md","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_outputs.ambr","tests/test_uc_surf_setup_ops_transcript.json"],"family":"deepseek","findings":3,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"d0ab1c4c0a648354","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B91e1d67c87.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261021T223202Z-df70618b.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5,6],"reviewed_head":"593e70d8bdaf92fb60b3db6c539b8d19d4f781d7","reviewed_paths":{"README.md":"100644 e0dc191db88a9367e41f052ed54738f08695f823","ddflow/api/briefing.py":"100644 c01e78e2b17358a4ff04b945a5add4480aa46863","ddflow/api/lifecycle/brief.py":"100644 cd153d55f4db3eaefe797eed0481be42b25b6268","ddflow/config_sections/session.py":"100644 bc20ddb18de48bfa57aef56e03b69d81e6df183c","ddflow/services/agent_brief.py":"100644 e7a2e8428dd0497a8af3575132a6fb3b8828c96c","ddflow/services/guidance/charter.py":"100644 e718a128162702d5233aac0d7f8494109a14acee","ddflow/services/guidance/inject.py":"100644 e7194e7db9bb09cc19311bf768c47b3c5e78e1d2","ddflow/templates/prompts/agent_brief.md":"100644 5af918bd7